{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A mother bear collects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fish. She gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fish to each of her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bear cubs. How many fish does the mother bear have left over?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663f3ef6f61359a657c27fea2c6228aabea512ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 0 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bear cubs and each is given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fish, they are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0f8037d7acb21e0c73e5ae336584073ac16b8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 3 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> fish in total.\n</p><p>Next, we see that she originally had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fish. Since she gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fish to the cubs, she had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/61587a661237f44e2de7fe3c099f996c1f584451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - 12 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" /> fish remaining.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Precede